{"slug": "jean-georges-vongerichtens-crab-salad", "nyt_id": 11175, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/11175-jean-georges-vongerichtens-crab-salad", "name": "Jean-Georges Vongerichten's Crab Salad", "author": "Molly O’Neill", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "6 servings", "min": 6, "max": 6, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 30, "raw": {"total": "About 30 minutes, plus refrigeration"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 cup minus 2 tablespoons all-purpose flour", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "minus 2 tablespoons all-purpose flour", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 ½ tablespoons sugar", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "sugar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "1 ½ tablespoons cumin seeds", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "cumin seeds", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "⅔ cup white-wine vinegar", "group": null, "quantity": 0.6666666666666666, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "white-wine vinegar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "1 ½ tablespoons melted butter", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "melted butter", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "3 tablespoons water", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "water", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "1 ½ pounds crab meat", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "lb", "item": "crab meat", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "2 small ripe tomatoes, cored and quartered", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "small ripe tomatoes", "preparation": "cored and quartered", "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "1 ½ shallots, peeled and coarsely chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "shallots", "preparation": "peeled and coarsely chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "1 large clove garlic, peeled and chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "large clove garlic", "preparation": "peeled and chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "1 ½ tablespoons lemon juice", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "lemon juice", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "3 tablespoons olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 13, "raw": "1 ½ tablespoons sherry vinegar", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "sherry vinegar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 14, "raw": "3 fresh basil leaves", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "fresh basil leaves", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 15, "raw": "Kosher salt and freshly ground black pepper to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "kosher salt and freshly ground black pepper to taste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 16, "raw": "2 bunches of mache, about 2 cups, rinsed", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "bunch", "item": "of mache", "preparation": "about 2 cups, rinsed", "optional": false}, {"position": 17, "raw": "1 ½ mangoes, peeled and cut into -inch dice", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "mangoes", "preparation": "peeled and cut into -inch dice", "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "To make the crisps, preheat the oven to 425 degrees. In a small bowl, mix together the flour, sugar and cumin seeds. Add the vinegar, butter and water and mix thoroughly, but do not overmix."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Working in batches and using a pastry brush, dab very thin 2-inch discs of batter onto a nonstick baking sheet. Bake until golden, 3 to 5 minutes. Cool on wire racks."}, {"position": 3, "text": "To make the crab salad, break up the lumps with your fingers, removing any shell or cartilage but leaving the crab as intact as possible. Refrigerate. In a blender, combine the tomatoes, shallots, garlic, lemon juice, oil, vinegar and basil and blend until smooth. Season to taste."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Slowly stir the tomato sauce into the crab meat. Coat the crab, but do not soak it. Place 3 scoops of crab salad on each of 6 plates. Place a cumin crisp between each scoop. Garnish with the mache and the mangoes."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 285.7, "protein_g": 23.0, "carbohydrates_g": 23.5, "fat_g": 11.4, "saturated_fat_g": 3.1, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 117.6, "sodium_mg": 831.8, "fiber_g": 3.3, "sugar_g": 17.3, "unsaturated_fat_g": 7.6, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": [], "course": ["appetizer"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["bake", "crab", "salad", "seafood"]}, "images": [], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 41}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "1997-10-19", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T23:01:26.126578+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "jean-georges-vongerichtens-crispy-aromatic-duck", "nyt_id": 11233, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/11233-jean-georges-vongerichtens-crispy-aromatic-duck", "name": "Jean-Georges Vongerichten's Crispy Aromatic Duck", "author": "Jonathan Reynolds", "description": "This recipe came to The Times from the chef Jean-Georges Vongerichten, who served it at 66 in New York. It takes a little unattended prep time and commitment, but the results are tender and fragrant and practically fall off the bone. The duck marinates in a spice rub in the fridge overnight, and then is steamed, quartered and fried. Serve it with Chinese pancakes, hoisin sauce and scallions.", "servings": {"text": "4 to 6 servings", "min": 4, "max": 6, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 300, "raw": {"total": "5 hours, plus refrigeration time"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "16-pound duck", "group": null, "quantity": 16.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "-pound duck", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "⅔ cup kosher salt", "group": null, "quantity": 0.6666666666666666, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "kosher salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "¼ cup black peppercorns", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "black peppercorns", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "5 tablespoons Sichuan peppercorns", "group": null, "quantity": 5.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "sichuan peppercorns", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "3 tablespoons cumin seeds", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "cumin seeds", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "2 tablespoons five-spice powder", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "five-spice powder", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "63-by- ⅛-inch slices peeled fresh ginger root", "group": null, "quantity": 63.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "-by- ⅛-inch slices peeled fresh ginger root", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "12 scallions, 6 cut into 3-inch lengths, 6 finely shredded", "group": null, "quantity": 12.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "scallions", "preparation": "6 cut into 3-inch lengths, 6 finely shredded", "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "Flour for dusting", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "flour for dusting", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "1 to 2 cups peanut oil", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": 2.0, "unit": "cup", "item": "peanut oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "Chinese mandarin pancakes (see note)", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "chinese mandarin pancakes (see note)", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "Hoisin sauce", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "hoisin sauce", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Rinse and dry the duck. Rub it inside and out with a mixture of salt, peppercorns, cumin and spice powder, then refrigerate in a plastic bag overnight."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Brush the spices off the duck and stuff the ginger and 3-inch lengths of scallion into the cavity. Steam, covered, for 2 hours, adding boiling water as necessary."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Remove the duck and discard the ginger and scallions. Cool until dry, about 2 hours."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Cut the duck into quarters, dust with flour and shake off excess. Fry the legs and thighs in peanut oil for 12 to 15 minutes, breasts 8 to 10 minutes, until crisp. Drain, and when cool, shred the meat with a fork."}, {"position": 5, "text": "To serve, brush each pancake with hoisin to taste, add some shredded duck and scallions and roll up as for Peking duck."}], "nutrition": null, "tags": {"cuisine": ["chinese"], "diet": [], "course": ["main course"], "meal": ["dinner"], "occasion": [], "other": ["duck", "fry"]}, "images": [], "rating": {"average": 3.0, "count": 7}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2003-01-05", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T02:09:55.988196+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "jean-georges-vongerichtens-gingered-beet-salad", "nyt_id": 6043, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/6043-jean-georges-vongerichtens-gingered-beet-salad", "name": "Jean-Georges Vongerichten's Gingered-Beet Salad", "author": "Molly O’Neill", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "Four servings", "min": 4, "max": 4, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 120, "raw": {"total": "2 hours"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "4 medium beets, scrubbed well", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "medium beets", "preparation": "scrubbed well", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 pound large shrimps, shelled", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "lb", "item": "large shrimps", "preparation": "shelled", "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "3 tablespoons canola oil", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "canola oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "1 2-inch piece ginger, peeled and grated", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "2-inch piece ginger", "preparation": "peeled and grated", "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "4 tablespoons sherry vinegar", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "sherry vinegar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "2 teaspoons salt", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "Freshly ground black pepper to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "freshly ground black pepper to taste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "2 tablespoons ½-inch-length chives", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "½-inch-length chives", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Preheat the oven to 350 degrees. Wrap the beets in two layers of aluminum foil and roast until fork-tender, about 1 hour and 45 minutes. Cool, peel and cut the beets into ½-inch sticks."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Toss the shrimps in a mixture made from 1 tablespoon of the oil, half of the grated ginger and 1 tablespoon of the vinegar. Marinate for 1 hour."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Heat the grill. Sprinkle the shrimps with 1 teaspoon of the salt and pepper to taste. Grill until just opaque, about 5 minutes."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Drizzle the beets with the remaining oil, ginger and vinegar. Add the chives, the remaining salt and pepper to taste. Serve with the grilled shrimp."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 216.4, "protein_g": 16.9, "carbohydrates_g": 10.0, "fat_g": 11.8, "saturated_fat_g": 1.1, "trans_fat_g": 0.1, "cholesterol_mg": 142.9, "sodium_mg": 706.8, "fiber_g": 2.6, "sugar_g": 5.6, "unsaturated_fat_g": 10.2, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": [], "course": ["appetizer"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["beet", "ginger", "grill", "marinate", "roast", "shrimp"]}, "images": [], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 5}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "1997-09-21", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T00:48:56.052991+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "jean-georges-vongerichtens-squash-on-toast", "nyt_id": 12944, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/12944-jean-georges-vongerichtens-squash-on-toast", "name": "Jean-Georges Vongerichten’s Squash on Toast", "author": "Mark Bittman", "description": "This appetizer takes a little effort, but it rewards with layers of rich fall flavor and texture. You’ll roast a cut squash and confit onion slices with maple syrup and apple cider vinegar. Veteran cooks will immediately get the idea: Cook the onions awhile, until they’re dark and soft, then add the two liquids and continue to cook until they’re jammy. The process could take as long as an hour, depending on the heat, your attentiveness and the water content of the onions. But it isn’t difficult. Do not forget the mint; it’s not the same without it. (The New York Times)", "servings": {"text": "4 to 8 servings", "min": 4, "max": 8, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 60, "raw": {"total": "About an hour"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 2 ½- to 3-pound kabocha or other yellow-fleshed squash, peeled, seeded and cut into pieces ⅛- to ¼-inch thick", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "2 ½- to 3-pound kabocha or other yellow-fleshed squash", "preparation": "peeled, seeded and cut into pieces ⅛- to ¼-inch thick", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "¾ cup extra-virgin olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 0.75, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "extra-virgin olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "½ teaspoon dried chile flakes, more to taste", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "dried chile flakes", "preparation": "more to taste", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "3 teaspoons kosher salt", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "kosher salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "1 yellow onion, peeled and thinly sliced", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "yellow onion", "preparation": "peeled and thinly sliced", "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "¼ cup apple cider vinegar", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "apple cider vinegar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "¼ cup maple syrup", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "maple syrup", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "4 slices country bread, 1-inch thick", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "slice", "item": "country bread", "preparation": "1-inch thick", "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "½ cup ricotta, goat cheese, feta or mascarpone", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "ricotta", "preparation": "goat cheese, feta or mascarpone", "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "Coarse salt", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "coarse salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "4 tablespoons chopped mint", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "chopped mint", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Heat the oven to 450. Combine the squash, ¼ cup olive oil, chile flakes and 2 teaspoons of salt in a bowl and toss well. Transfer the mixture to a parchment-lined baking sheet and cook, stirring every few minutes, until tender and slightly colored, about 15 minutes or a little longer. Remove from the oven."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Meanwhile, heat another ¼ cup olive oil over medium-high heat, add the onions and remaining teaspoon salt and cook, stirring frequently, until the onions are well softened and darkening, at least 15 minutes. Add the vinegar and syrup, stir and reduce until syrupy and broken down, again at least 15 minutes or so; the mixture should be jammy."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Combine squash and onions in a bowl and smash with a fork until combined. Taste for seasoning."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Add the remaining oil to a skillet over medium-high heat. Working in batches if necessary, add bread and cook until just golden on both sides, less than 10 minutes total; drain on paper towels. Spread cheese on toasts, then top with the squash-onion mixture. Sprinkle with coarse salt and garnish with mint."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 398.1, "protein_g": 4.6, "carbohydrates_g": 29.4, "fat_g": 30.1, "saturated_fat_g": 5.2, "trans_fat_g": 0.1, "cholesterol_mg": 10.1, "sodium_mg": 434.2, "fiber_g": 2.5, "sugar_g": 10.0, "unsaturated_fat_g": 23.7, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": ["vegetarian"], "course": ["appetizer", "side dish"], "meal": [], "occasion": ["thanksgiving"], "other": ["bake", "fall", "ricotta", "saute", "squash", "winter"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2015/11/16/dining/16COOKING-SQUASHONTOAST/16COOKING-SQUASHONTOAST-facebookJumbo.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}], "rating": {"average": 5.0, "count": 860}, "video_url": "https://www.nytimes.com/video/dining/100000001900055/squash-toast.html", "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2012-11-14", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T00:02:44.237051+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "jean-georgess-sesame-noodles", "nyt_id": 11232, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/11232-jean-georgess-sesame-noodles", "name": "Jean-Georges's Sesame Noodles", "author": "Jonathan Reynolds", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "4 servings", "min": 4, "max": 4, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 75, "raw": {"total": "1 hour 15 minutes"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "½ cup soy sauce", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "soy sauce", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "¼ cup black vinegar", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "black vinegar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "¼ cup rice vinegar", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "rice vinegar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "¼ cup shao shing wine", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "shao shing wine", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "½ cup sugar", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "sugar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "1 ounce fresh cilantro", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "oz", "item": "fresh cilantro", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "½ hot red chili", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "hot red chili", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "1 cinnamon stick, crushed", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "cinnamon stick", "preparation": "crushed", "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "1 tablespoon coriander seeds", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "coriander seeds", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "1 tablespoon sugar", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "sugar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "1 teaspoon puréed fresh ginger root", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "puréed fresh ginger root", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "½ teaspoon puréed garlic", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "puréed garlic", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 13, "raw": "1 Thai chili, broken into small pieces", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "thai chili", "preparation": "broken into small pieces", "optional": false}, {"position": 14, "raw": "¾ cup toasted peanuts, chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 0.75, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "toasted peanuts", "preparation": "chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 15, "raw": "¾ cup toasted sesame seeds", "group": null, "quantity": 0.75, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "toasted sesame seeds", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 16, "raw": "Dark sesame oil", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "dark sesame oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 17, "raw": "Peanut oil", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "peanut oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 18, "raw": "Salt to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt to taste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 19, "raw": "Cayenne pepper to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "cayenne pepper to taste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 20, "raw": "5 ounces bean-paste", "group": null, "quantity": 5.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "oz", "item": "bean-paste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 21, "raw": "vermicelli noodles", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "vermicelli noodles", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 22, "raw": "9 tablespoons sugar", "group": null, "quantity": 9.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "sugar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 23, "raw": "4 tablespoons wasabi powder", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "wasabi powder", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 24, "raw": "Slivered apples, cucumbers, scallions and fresh bean sprouts", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "slivered apples", "preparation": "cucumbers, scallions and fresh bean sprouts", "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "To make the broth, boil the soy sauce, vinegars, wine and sugar, stirring to dissolve. Add the remaining ingredients and steep, covered, 45 minutes."}, {"position": 2, "text": "To make the paste, sauté the sugar, ginger, garlic and chili until it is coated with melted sugar and caramelized. Reserve 2 tablespoons each peanuts and sesame seeds for garnish and blend the remainder in a food processor with the ginger mixture, adding the oils to make a paste. Season with salt and cayenne."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Cover the noodles with 1 quart boiling water and stir until loosened. Set aside until tender, about 15 minutes. Drain."}, {"position": 4, "text": "To make the crystallized wasabi, mix the sugar and wasabi powder thoroughly, then add 5 to 6 teaspoons cold water until ''pebbles'' form."}, {"position": 5, "text": "To serve, spoon ¼ cup broth into each of 4 shallow serving bowls. Add ⅛ of the noodles, the paste and the garnishes, including the peanuts and seeds, then Re